<%- include('header', { pageTitle: 'Terms' }) %>
<section class="narrow prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated 12 September 2026</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
        <%= brand %> is a free hobby service run by one person on their own
        hardware. Be decent, do not upload things you have no right to upload,
        and keep your own backups of anything you would be upset to lose.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
        You are responsible for what happens under your account and for keeping
        your password to yourself. You must be old enough to consent to data
        processing where you live (16 in Hungary).
    </p>

    <h2>What you upload</h2>
    <p>
        You keep ownership of everything you write and upload. By publishing a
        list you allow the service to display that content to whoever opens the
        page — nothing more.
    </p>
    <p>Do not upload content that:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>you do not hold the rights to;</li>
        <li>is illegal, or depicts abuse of any kind;</li>
        <li>harasses, impersonates or exposes another person;</li>
        <li>exists to advertise, spam or mislead.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Accounts posting such material may be removed without notice. Report
        anything that needs attention through the contact route on the
        <a href="<%= u('/privacy') %>">privacy page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
        Each account gets <%= quotaMb %> MB of photo storage and a cap on photos
        per adventure. These exist to keep a small server usable for everyone
        and may change.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
        The service is provided as-is, with no guarantee of availability or of
        data preservation. It may go down, change or shut down. Backups are
        taken, but export your data from
        <a href="<%= u('/settings') %>">Settings</a> if it matters to you. To the extent the
        law allows, the operator is not liable for losses arising from use of
        the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending it</h2>
    <p>
        Delete your account whenever you like from
        <a href="<%= u('/settings') %>">Settings</a>; it takes effect immediately. The
        operator may close accounts that break these terms.
    </p>

    <p class="note">
        The source code is open under the MIT licence, which covers the code —
        not this hosted service.
    </p>
</section>
<%- include('footer') %>
